# SABOTAGE: T126 — the ConfirmLive double-mount consume guard (P0, T113-caused).
# Since ADR-042 the LiveSocket client ships, so `GET /verify/:token` mounts TWICE
# in a browser: the disconnected (dead) HTTP render, then the connected socket
# join. `Samen.Web.Auth.ConfirmLive` consumes a single-use `:email_verify` token
# ON MOUNT. Pre-T126 it consumed on EVERY mount: the dead render consumed the
# token (success) and the connected re-mount re-consumed the now-spent token
# (`{:error, :invalid_token}`) — the connected render is authoritative, so a real
# user saw a FALSE "Couldn't verify this link" even though the account WAS
# verified server-side (the T49 dogfood re-walk regression). The T126 fix runs
# the consume EXACTLY ONCE on the dead render, then redirects to a NON-secret
# `?verified=1` / `?error=invalid_token` status flag — so no socket connects to
# `/verify/:token` and the connected mount never re-consumes.
#
# This sabotage removes the redirect guard: consume-and-render on EVERY mount
# (the exact pre-fix regression). The named regression test — which asserts the
# dead mount REDIRECTS to `?verified=1` (never renders the token clause inline) —
# MUST fail. Revert restores the guard byte-exact.
#
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/auth/confirm_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: REGRESSION (T126): the dead+connected double-mount verifies EXACTLY ONCE
diff --git a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/auth/confirm_live.ex b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/auth/confirm_live.ex
--- a/samen_web/lib/samen/web/auth/confirm_live.ex
+++ b/samen_web/lib/samen/web/auth/confirm_live.ex
@@ -55,14 +55,8 @@ defmodule Samen.Web.Auth.ConfirmLive do
   def mount(%{"token" => token}, session, socket) do
     socket = Samen.Web.Live.assign_mount(socket, session)
     mount = socket.assigns.samen_mount

-    # The ONE mutating consume, on the dead render only, then redirect to the
-    # status flag (see moduledoc "Double-mount guard").
-    flag =
-      case Confirm.consume(token, mods(mount)) do
-        {:ok, _} -> "verified=1"
-        {:error, :invalid_token} -> "error=invalid_token"
-      end
-
-    {:ok, redirect(socket, to: "#{verify_action(mount, token)}?#{flag}")}
+    # SABOTAGE (T126): double-mount guard removed — consume-and-render on every mount.
+    result = Confirm.consume(token, mods(mount))
+    {:ok, assign(socket, verified?: match?({:ok, _}, result), error: nil)}
   end
